  "methodology": "Fixed-position unit-peak restoring-beam fits with a local planar background on science images in Jy per beam. Control positions exclude nearby W-CDFS catalogue components and are separated by at least one restoring-beam major FWHM. Use the larger of the local and inner scaled MAD of controls and the supplied VLASS RMS map value when available. The 90 percent recovery amplitude adds a matching compact-source contribution to the measured control residuals. NVSS uses the survey beam; the map is reprojected by SkyView.",
  "limitation": "The W-CDFS and NVSS mosaics combine exposures from their survey intervals. The VLASS Quick Look epoch 1.1 has documented pointing and flux-scale issues. The broad NVSS and W-CDFS beams blend the transient coordinate and nearby galaxy. An independent counterpart during the 2026 JWST visits requires contemporaneous target data."
